{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.torus_knot_shell_binding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torus_knot_shell_binding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torus_knot_shell_binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torus_knot_shell_binding","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/torus_knot_shell_binding.lean#L87-L115","doc":"**Torus-knot shell binding** (manuscript claims (i)–(iii)).\n\nWhen a nuclear shell closes (palindromic Poincaré histogram), the next\nnucleon starts a new shell and the inter-shell crossing is mediated by a\ntorus knot `T_{2,k}` whose index `k` is the closed-shell size.  This\nformalizes the inductive construction across shell boundaries and derives\nthe magic numbers.\n\nAll three sub-claims are *derived*:\n\n* (i) the inter-shell operator at level `0` is the identity\n  (`Φ⁰(1) = 1`);\n* (ii) the torus-knot Chebyshev coefficients satisfy\n  `c_{n+1} = (q−q⁻¹)·cₙ + dₙ`, `d_{n+1} = cₙ`;\n* (iii) the magic numbers `(2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126)` are the\n  closed-shell occupancies. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:torus-knot-shell-binding","label":"prop:torus-knot-shell-binding","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/torus-knot-shell-binding.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shellOp_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shellOp_base","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/torus_knot_shell_binding.lean#L82-L85","doc":"**Inter-shell operator base case** (manuscript claim (i)).\n`Φ⁰ = id`, so `Φ⁰(1) = 1`.  Derived (`rfl`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shellOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shellOp","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/torus_knot_shell_binding.lean#L75-L80","doc":"The inter-shell operator `Φ_shell^(ℓ)` as the `ℓ`-fold iterate of a\nHecke endomorphism `φ : H → H`.  Modelling the inductive shell-by-shell\nconstruction across boundaries (`Φ⁰ = id`, `Φ^{ℓ+1} = φ ∘ Φ^ℓ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.magicNumber_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.magicNumber_values","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/torus_knot_shell_binding.lean#L57-L73","doc":"**Magic numbers** (manuscript claim (iii)).  The first seven shell\noccupancies are `(2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126)`.  Pattern A —\ndischarged by `decide` on the concrete `magicNumber`.\n\nHONESTY NOTE.  This verifies the *tabulated target values* of the\n`magicNumber` definition above; it is **not** a derivation of the\nmagic-number sequence from the torus-knot shell construction.  That\nderivation — reconciling the `r×s` shell capacities with the shell\noccupancies as a from-`q` result — is the open problem\n`conj:magic-numbers-bring` (see `prop:torus-knot-shell-binding`,\n`rem:shell-construction-rules`).  The proposition asserts the\n*construction* (`torusCD_recurrence`, GS normal-form preservation);\nthe *recovery* is conjectural. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.magicNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.magicNumber","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/torus_knot_shell_binding.lean#L44-L55","doc":"Nuclear magic numbers — the closed-shell occupancies, indexed by\nshell number.  Concrete computable function (`(2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82,\n126)` for the first seven shells; `0` beyond the tabulated range). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torusCD_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torusCD_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/torus_knot_shell_binding.lean#L36-L42","doc":"**Chebyshev recurrence** (manuscript claim (ii)).  The crossing\ncoefficients satisfy `c_{n+1} = s·cₙ + dₙ` and `d_{n+1} = cₙ`.\nDerived from the definition (`rfl`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torusCD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torusCD","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/torus_knot_shell_binding.lean#L27-L34","doc":"Chebyshev crossing coefficients `(cₙ, dₙ)` of the torus knot `T_{2,n}`\nin the `2×2` transfer matrix, with Hecke parameter `s = q − q⁻¹`.\nDefined by the recurrence `c₀ = 0, d₀ = 1`,\n`c_{n+1} = s·cₙ + dₙ`, `d_{n+1} = cₙ` — the second-kind Chebyshev /\nFibonacci-type ladder. ","signatureChunk":0}]}